"[2602.00276v1] Localizing and Correcting Errors for LLM-based Planners (https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.00276v1)\nciteturn25997view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.00276v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 30 Jan 2026 (this version), latest version 6 Sep 2026 (cite5†v3 )]\nL9: # Title:Localizing and Correcting Errors for LLM-based Planners\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Aditya Kumar , cite7†William W. Cohen L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Localizing and Correcting Errors for LLM-based Planners, by Aditya Kumar and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Large language models (LLMs) have demonstrated strong reasoning capabilities on math and coding, but frequently fail on symbolic classical planning tasks. Our studies, as well as prior work, show that LLM-generated plans routinely violate domain constraints given in their instructions (e.g., walking through walls). To address this failure, we propose iteratively augmenting instructions with Localized In-Context Learning (L-ICL) demonstrations: targeted corrections for specific failing steps.\nL17: Specifically, L-ICL identifies the first constraint violation in a trace and injects a minimal input-output example giving the correct behavior for the failing step. Our proposed technique of L-ICL is much effective than explicit instructions or traditional ICL, which adds complete problem-solving trajectories, and many other baselines. For example, on an 8x8 gridworld, L-ICL produces valid plans 89% of the time with only 60 training examples, compared to 59% for the best baseline, an increase of 30%.\nL18: L-ICL also shows dramatic improvements in other domains (gridworld navigation, mazes, Sokoban, and BlocksWorld), and on several LLM architectures.\nL19: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2602.00276 [cs.AI]\nL21:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2602.00276v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL22:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.00276†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: William Cohen [cite13†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Fri, 30 Jan 2026 19:56:15 UTC (1,405 KB)\nL27: cite14†[v2] Fri, 6 Mar 2026 17:37:41 UTC (1,405 KB)\nL28: cite5†[v3] Sun, 6 Sep 2026 01:55:04 UTC (351 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Localizing and Correcting Errors for LLM-based Planners, by Aditya Kumar and 1 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite8†View PDF L37:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite15†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite16†view license†creativecommons.org L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.AI\nL44: \nL45: cite17†< prev |   cite18†next > L46: \nL47: cite19†new | cite20†recent | cite21†2026-02 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite22†cs L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite25†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmark\nL70: \nL71: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL72: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL75: \nL76: Bibliographic Explorer (cite26†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL77: \nL78: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL79: \n